{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for the sole bound artifact notes/2026-10-16-repo-in-ai-mvp-plan.md at 206a1b8ddc254278acfb43c7f725acd96261012c, tree250702483fea41eb955bbd988be5bd68807e5d31. The local-only experiment, existing coding agents, open MCP Apps boundary, Claude stdio primary route, ChatGPT probe/fallback, and ordering after the existing sequence are sound choices. These findings concern the executable plan, not a request to build more of the hosted product.\n\nF1 high — Make the founding authority and the counted approval in section1.4/S1/S3 explicit. The two members created as agents do not receive change.review (packages/platform/src/membership.ts:100-107,144-165,414-445). Moreover the other contributing agent is among the integrated manifest's authors, and review-verdict refuses author-cannot-review (change.ts:927-929); granting it review would not fix independence. Specify who supplies the one counted approval, and the ownerMayReview/controller policy if the single owner is to approve their agents' work (reservation.ts:237-246). The smallest existing-authority option may be owner review and merge under an explicit permitted rules configuration; keep agent feedback distinct from counted approval. Also name how S1 grants the new issue.decide to the intended person roles, using reviewed founding configuration such as existing set-actions if appropriate, while excluding agent and checker roles. Adding an issue act alone supplies no membership grant. Witness the whole scenario with real membership/rules, including the agent refusal and an approval the actual destination counts.\n\nF2 high — Carry changed criteria through the work rather than relabelling old commitments/reports as new. Section1.4 revises the intent after both commitments were accepted, but commitment conditionsAt/termsAt are fixed (issue.ts:63-66), offer snapshots them (350-360), revise updates only the intent (239-253), and report takes conditionsAt from its commitment and validates that commitment's terms (551-575). The native objects do not acquire the newly decided criteria automatically. Specify the existing cancellation/new-offer or other deliberately reviewed adoption path, or explicitly retain old work as old-version input with a recorded acceptance relation. Show current intent criteria, agreed commitment terms, report terms and decide.criteriaAt separately. Witness both agents resuming against the selected terms and prevent the Change view from presenting an old-terms report as evidence of agreement to the new criteria. No retroactive mutation of old signed commitments is requested.\n\nF3 high — Keep candidate test code outside the checker's signing and desktop authority boundary in S7. The planned script both executes candidate node tests and holds a checker signer. Checkout integrity proves which program ran, not that it cannot read DAP_HOME, alter the bare destination or fabricate a result. The reviewed runner contract explicitly treats the tree as untrusted and excludes signing keys and writes outside the runner (packages/checkers/src/runner.ts:32-40; sandbox.ts:7-33; signing.ts:10-19). Plan a concrete local execution boundary with the signer and room credentials outside it, bounded execution and a job/tree/configuration-bound result through the existing service/signing path. Alternatively explicitly limit this experiment to separately reviewed, trusted fixture code and describe the result as trusted member execution, not preservation of the runner isolation contract; do not automatically execute arbitrary new candidate tests on the owner's desktop. Witness the selected boundary, including unsuccessful key/home/destination access if claiming isolation. No deployment is needed to state or implement a local boundary.\n\nF4 medium — Make owner-only signer access an S0 acceptance condition, not merely tunnel connectivity. dap mcp selects one signer before serving (mcp.ts:77-102); a caller reaching that process can therefore ask it to sign as that owner. A private tunnel or a host write prompt is not by itself per-person signer authentication. OpenAI's current tunnel documentation describes Platform-organization and ChatGPT-workspace associations, separate Manage/Use permissions and a runtime API key; it does not establish exclusive access by one person. Use a dedicated test-room configuration/key, state the intended allowed caller contexts, and require denial outside them before connecting an owner-capable process. Do not fix an HTTP failure by dropping the loopback bearer or Origin refusal. A safe probe can use a throwaway signer/write tool, as already proposed. If owner-only routing cannot be established, keep ChatGPT at the stated fallback. Also correct H1's categorical 'Both hosts require [OAuth]': the cited current Claude authentication page explicitly supports no auth and limited static-header auth, and OpenAI custom-server docs allow no auth. OAuth is the proposed authenticated multi-user route, not a universal host connectivity requirement. Sources checked16Oct: https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/secure-mcp-tunnels ; https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/custom-mcp-server ; https://claude.com/docs/connectors/building/authentication .\n\nF5 medium — Specify how the killed-session recovery in1.5/S5 is authorized. offer-handover can be signed only by the current performer (issue.ts:447-454), and accept-handover requires its named successor plus no live hold (459-467). Killing a session does not offer a handover, end a hold immediately or authorize an unrelated successor. Choose and witness the actual sequence: restart the same member/key and continue, arrange a handover before the kill, or provide a separately authorized recovery path. Reusing the existing key in a fresh session is a valid smaller experiment, but label that as same-identity restart rather than proof of a new-member handover. Include the hold-ending step/time and the original block/decision references. No broad takeover permission is requested.\n\nF6 medium — Complete the context read and Decision-view slice needed for the no-copy proof. The gap table correctly marks both diff and file reads missing, but S6 commissions only diff. A brief unchanged between base and integration never appears in that diff, and a path+commit or evidence digest in S3 is not its content. State the bounded, authorized exact-commit file/evidence read used by the host and where the substantive Decision view renders goal, alternatives, consequences, recommendation, brief and adopted criteria and invokes decide. Use the native content/source bindings rather than a parallel store. Witness a fresh conversation recovering an unchanged brief and decision evidence through MCP, and distinguish the owner's/model's semantic comparison from a native check that automatically detects product conflicts. If S0 falls back to one host, mark the two-host pass item pending rather than requiring S8 to claim all six passed.\n\nArchitecture conclusion: direction supported; changes requested on native authority, criteria provenance, recovery and complete read/view dependencies. Security conclusion: changes requested on S7 execution isolation/trust scope and S0 access to the fixed owner signer. Simplification conclusion: preserve the one-repository, local-only and existing-record choices; solve these with explicit existing grants/terms/restart choices and bounded read surfaces before inventing new authorities or stores. Persistent operation custody for the new on-disk port should also be witnessed at a lost-reply/restart boundary so the already-promised no-repeat property is tested beyond a normal restart.\n\nValidation: read the complete bound note and checked the cited native boundaries at its exact Git head. Independent Git comparison against54dcefbc shows one added Markdown file only; relative link resolves and git diff --check is clean. Verified primary external documentation for the tunnel, custom MCP access, desktop-only route, Claude stdio/domain restrictions, stable2026-01-26 MCP Apps metadata/CSP, basic-host and Inspector. ext-apps2.0.3 (25Sep), Inspector2.11.0 and Workers OAuth provider1.2.3 (7Oct) versions match their maintainers' current manifests/releases. No actual host/account probe, native MVP run, implementation commission or runtime approval is claimed. No source/tests changed, so no gate repeated for this prose-only candidate under docs/testing.md. No private logs, credentials, package install, push or deployment.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:67e11d92aa3c4f2fd849e4d9060ccc82727f30f6","binding":"assigned","head":"206a1b8ddc254278acfb43c7f725acd96261012c","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2b1b0d81b45537f9f75f4e644008d7becd388e95\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:437379213232e582a8121ba398e1eea6f9ee5385\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3d1dbdbd1e0ab9fef3d2fdb5545e9b2937fabb0a","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}